1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:04,220
Procure Flow now helps you request quantities that suppliers can fulfil as

2
00:00:04,240 --> 00:00:08,340
full bales or cartons. The selected supplier's pack size follows the request

3
00:00:08,360 --> 00:00:11,960
through approval, purchasing and receiving. Here's how to use it.

4
00:00:13,225 --> 00:00:17,085
Start in Create Request, or select a supplier offer from Supplier Stock.

5
00:00:17,885 --> 00:00:21,145
Confirm the supplier and product, then check the bale or carton size

6
00:00:21,165 --> 00:00:24,765
shown for that item. Another supplier may use a different pack size.

7
00:00:25,675 --> 00:00:29,635
With thirty units per pack, entering thirty one adjusts the request to

8
00:00:29,655 --> 00:00:31,635
sixty when you leave the quantity field.

9
00:00:32,275 --> 00:00:34,235
The adjustment message explains the change.

10
00:00:34,655 --> 00:00:37,175
Plus and minus controls move by one full pack.

11
00:00:37,715 --> 00:00:40,035
Review the new quantity and recalculated totals.

12
00:00:41,655 --> 00:00:45,495
Check the receiving site, each line's need by date, price and total.

13
00:00:46,255 --> 00:00:47,755
Save Draft keeps your work for later.

14
00:00:48,575 --> 00:00:51,555
If an older draft contains an odd quantity, correct it to a

15
00:00:51,575 --> 00:00:53,175
full pack before saving or submitting.

16
00:00:53,195 --> 00:00:56,175
Follow the existing approval and Concur handover.

17
00:00:57,050 --> 00:01:01,070
If the bale or carton size is unconfirmed, new ordering is blocked.

18
00:01:01,790 --> 00:01:05,530
Ask Procurement to confirm the supplier pack data, then refresh and try

19
00:01:05,550 --> 00:01:07,390
again. Do not guess a size.

20
00:01:07,750 --> 00:01:10,550
A supplier confirmed pack of one allows loose units.

21
00:01:12,002 --> 00:01:14,862
Open Request Details to see the saved pack size and number of

22
00:01:14,882 --> 00:01:18,722
full packs. These details remain with the order when supplier data changes

23
00:01:18,742 --> 00:01:21,902
later. Finance and line reports retain the same context.

24
00:01:21,922 --> 00:01:25,462
Older orders with no recorded pack are labelled as legacy.

25
00:01:26,592 --> 00:01:30,472
In Record Delivery, enter the units actually delivered, even when a carton

26
00:01:30,492 --> 00:01:33,692
is incomplete. A delivery of seven units stays seven.

27
00:01:34,312 --> 00:01:38,032
Use Add Unplanned Item for goods outside the original order, and follow

28
00:01:38,052 --> 00:01:39,652
the existing variance process.

29
00:01:41,280 --> 00:01:44,520
Before submitting, confirm the supplier, pack size, adjusted quantity and total.

30
00:01:45,220 --> 00:01:48,620
During receiving, record actual units. Pack counts explain the order;

31
00:01:49,180 --> 00:01:51,940
they do not replace unit quantities or prices in Concur.

32
00:01:52,260 --> 00:01:54,520
Use the feature guide whenever you need a reminder.
